    "markdown": "![Hugging Face's logo](https://huggingface.co/front/assets/huggingface_logo-noborder.svg) Hugging Face⟨1⟩\n  *  Models ⟨2⟩\n  *  Datasets ⟨3⟩\n  *  Spaces ⟨4⟩\n  *  Buckets new⟨5⟩\n  *  Docs ⟨6⟩\n  *  Enterprise ⟨7⟩\n  * Pricing⟨8⟩\n  *     * Website\n      *  Tasks⟨9⟩\n      *  HuggingChat⟨10⟩\n      *  Collections⟨11⟩\n      *  Languages⟨12⟩\n      *  Organizations⟨13⟩\n    * Community\n      *  Blog⟨14⟩\n      *  Posts⟨15⟩\n      *  Daily Papers⟨16⟩\n      *  Hardware⟨17⟩\n      *  Learn⟨18⟩\n      *  Discord⟨19⟩\n      *  Forum⟨20⟩\n      *  GitHub⟨21⟩\n    * Solutions\n      *  Team & Enterprise⟨7⟩\n      *  Hugging Face PRO⟨22⟩\n      *  Enterprise Support⟨23⟩\n      *  Inference Providers⟨24⟩\n      *  Inference Endpoints⟨25⟩\n      *  Storage Buckets⟨5⟩\n  * * * *\n  * Log In⟨26⟩\n  * Sign Up⟨27⟩\n\n\n#   Datasets:⟨3⟩\n* * *\nDuplicated from jessezhaoxizhang/RepoZero-C2Rust⟨28⟩\n![⟨29⟩]\n ![](https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/675590a59b57b4baf0c398e8/LA-f-5S1ByIlahLM6lwLP.png) ⟨30⟩\nPKU-Wu-Lab⟨30⟩\n/\nRepoZero-C2Rust⟨31⟩\nlike 0\nFollow\n![⟨32⟩] PKU-ICL-WuLab 4\nArXiv:\narxiv: 2605.07122\n Dataset card ⟨31⟩ Files Files and versions xet ⟨33⟩ Community ⟨34⟩\nDataset Viewer\nThe dataset viewer is not available because its heuristics could not detect any supported data files⟨35⟩. You can try uploading⟨36⟩ some data files, or configuring⟨37⟩ the data files location manually.\n**YAML Metadata Warning:** empty or missing yaml metadata in repo card\nCheck out the documentation⟨38⟩ for more information.\n  * Overview⟨39⟩\n  * Task Description⟨40⟩\n  * Libraries⟨41⟩\n  * Directory Structure⟨42⟩\n  * Data Format⟨43⟩\n    * Source Files⟨44⟩\n    * Test Cases⟨45⟩\n  * Installation⟨46⟩\n  * Metrics⟨47⟩\n  * Docker Environment⟨48⟩\n  * License⟨49⟩\n  * Citation⟨50⟩\n  * Related⟨51⟩\n\n\n#   ⟨52⟩ RepoZero-C2Rust \n ![RepoZero](https://huggingface.co/datasets/PKU-Wu-Lab/RepoZero-C2Rust/resolve/main/icon_repozero.png) ⟨53⟩\n![arXiv](https://img.shields.io/badge/RepoZero-arxiv-red)⟨54⟩ ![code](https://img.shields.io/badge/github-repo-blue?logo=github)⟨53⟩ ![HuggingFace-C2Rust](https://img.shields.io/badge/C2Rust-HF-yellow?logo=huggingface)⟨55⟩ ![HuggingFace-Py2JS](https://img.shields.io/badge/Py2JS-HF-yellow?logo=huggingface)⟨56⟩ ![Project Page](https://img.shields.io/badge/Homepage-gray?logo=homepage)⟨57⟩\nRepoZero-C2Rust is a benchmark subset for evaluating **zero-shot C++ to Rust repository-level code translation**.\n##   ⟨39⟩ Overview   \n| Property  | Value  |  \n| --- | --- |  \n| **Source Language**  | C++  |  \n| **Target Language**  | Rust  |  \n| **Number of Libraries**  | 11  |  \n| **Total Test Files**  | 200  |  \n| **HuggingFace Dataset**  | jessezhaoxizhang/RepoZero-C2Rust⟨28⟩  |  \n##   ⟨40⟩ Task Description \nGiven a C++ library implementation, the model must translate it into idiomatic, correct Rust code that:\n  * Re-implements the library logic using Rust-native idioms and standard crates\n  * Matches the I/O behavior of the original C++ test programs exactly\n  * Avoids directly wrapping the C++ source (zero-shot black-box translation)\n\n\n##   ⟨41⟩ Libraries   \n| Library  | Description  | Domain  |  \n| --- | --- | --- |  \n| **Clipper**  | Polygon clipping library  | Computational Geometry  |  \n| **color**  | Color manipulation utilities  | Graphics  |  \n| **earcut.hpp**  | Polygon triangulation  | Computational Geometry  |  \n| **exprtk**  | Mathematical expression parser  | Parsing  |  \n| **hopscotch-map**  | Fast hash map implementation  | Data Structures  |  \n| **idna-cpp**  | Internationalized Domain Names processing  | Networking  |  \n| **immer**  | Immutable data structures  | Data Structures  |  \n| **indicators**  | Terminal progress indicators  | CLI  |  \n| **inflection-cpp**  | String inflection library  | Text Processing  |  \n| **sortedcontainers-cpp**  | Sorted container implementations  | Data Structures  |  \n| **url-parser**  | URL parsing library  | Networking  |  \n##   ⟨42⟩ Directory Structure \n\n```\nC2Rust/\n├── CppLarge/                    # C++ source libraries (11 repos)\n│   ├── Clipper/\n│   ├── color/\n│   ├── earcut.hpp/\n│   ├── exprtk/\n│   ├── hopscotch-map/\n│   ├── idna-cpp/\n│   ├── immer/\n│   ├── indicators/\n│   ├── inflection-cpp/\n│   ├── sortedcontainers-cpp/\n│   └── url-parser/\n├── api_lines.jsonl              # API line counts\n├── cleaned_test_cases.jsonl     # Test case parameters for evaluation\n└── recompile_all.sh             # Script to recompile C++ executables\n\n```\n\n##   ⟨43⟩ Data Format \n###   ⟨44⟩ Source Files \nEach library in `CppLarge/` contains:\n  * C++ source files (`.cpp`, `.hpp`)\n  * Pre-compiled test executables\n  * Test input files\n\n\n###   ⟨45⟩ Test Cases \n`cleaned_test_cases.jsonl` contains test case parameters in JSONL format:\n\n```\n{\"filename\": \"Clipper/test1\", \"input\": \"...\", \"expected_output\": \"...\"}\n\n```\n\n##   ⟨46⟩ Installation \n\n```\ngit clone https://github.com/JesseZZZZZ/RepoZero.git\ncd RepoZero\npip install -r requirements.txt\n# This will download the HuggingFace dataset\npython download_dataset.py\n\n```\n\n##   ⟨47⟩ Metrics   \n| Metric  | Description  |  \n| --- | --- |  \n| **All-Pass Rate**  | Fraction of source files where _all_ test cases pass  |  \n| **Test-Case Pass Rate**  | Mean per-file fraction of passing test cases  |  \n##   ⟨48⟩ Docker Environment \nEach evaluation task runs in an isolated container with:\n  * **Workspace** : `/workspace`\n  * **Dataset** : `/workspace/dataset` (C++ sources + pre-compiled executables)\n  * **Output** : `/output` (generated Rust files)\n  * **Rust Toolchain** : Latest stable Rust with cargo\n  * **Network** : Disabled (`--network none`) for security\n\n\n##   ⟨49⟩ License \nDataset and code are released under Apache 2.0. All source code used in the benchmark is derived from open-source repositories; their original licenses remain in effect within their respective directories.\n##   ⟨50⟩ Citation \nIf you use RepoZero-C2Rust in your research, please cite:\n\n```\n@article{zhang2026repozero,\n  title={RepoZero: Can LLMs Generate a Code Repository from Scratch?},\n  author={Zhang, Zhaoxi and Xu, Yiming and Li, Weikang and Liang, Jiahui and Wu, Yunfang},\n  journal={arXiv preprint arXiv:2605.07122},\n  year={2026}\n}\n\n```\n\n##   ⟨51⟩ Related \n  * RepoZero Main Repository⟨53⟩\n  * Project Homepage⟨57⟩\n\n\nCopy to bucket new \n\nDownloads last month\n    665\nTotal file size: 12.5 MB\n##  Collection including PKU-Wu-Lab/RepoZero-C2Rust\n#### RepoZero Collection A collection of RepoZero benchmark • 2 items • Updated 10 days ago • 1 ⟨58⟩\n##  Paper for PKU-Wu-Lab/RepoZero-C2Rust\n#### RepoZero: Can LLMs Generate a Code Repository from Scratch? Paper • 2605.07122 • Published May 20 ⟨59⟩\nSystem theme\nCompany\nTOS⟨60⟩ Privacy⟨61⟩ About⟨62⟩ Careers⟨63⟩ ⟨1⟩\nWebsite\nModels⟨2⟩ Datasets⟨3⟩ Spaces⟨4⟩ Pricing⟨8⟩ Docs⟨6⟩\n",
